# Vue.js 3 + Vite + Tailwind CSS

## Technology Stack

- **Vue 3.5+** with Composition API (`<script setup>`) — no Options API in new code. Use `defineModel()` and `useTemplateRef()`.
- **TypeScript** strict mode (`"strict": true` in `tsconfig.json`).
- **Vite** as build tool — leverage HMR and lazy loading.
- **Tailwind CSS v4** — CSS-first (`@import "tailwindcss"`, `@theme`). No `tailwind.config.*` unless you have a documented exception.
- **oxlint** as the primary linter; ESLint only for rules oxlint does not cover.
- **Pinia** for global state (replaces Vuex).
- **Vue Router 4** for routing.
- **VueUse** for composable utilities — prefer over custom implementations.

## Project Structure

In a web application with a separate backend, the Vue.js project lives in `frontend/`
at the project root (see `06-project-structure.mdc` — web application layout).
The `src/` below is the internal Vite layout inside `frontend/`.

```
frontend/
├── src/
│   ├── assets/       # Static files
│   ├── components/   # Reusable components (atomic)
│   │   ├── ui/       # Generic UI elements (Button, Input, Modal…)
│   │   └── features/ # Domain-specific components
│   ├── composables/  # Shared logic (use*.ts)
│   ├── layouts/      # Layout components (DefaultLayout, AuthLayout)
│   ├── pages/        # Route components (1 page = 1 file)
│   ├── router/       # Vue Router configuration
│   ├── stores/       # Pinia stores
│   ├── types/        # Shared TypeScript types
│   └── utils/        # Helper functions
├── Dockerfile
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
└── vite.config.ts
```

## Components

```vue
<!-- ✅ Correct pattern — <script setup> with TypeScript -->
<script setup lang="ts">
import { computed } from 'vue'
import type { User } from '@/types/user'

const user = defineModel<User>('user', { required: true })
const isLoading = defineModel<boolean>('isLoading', { default: false })
const emit = defineEmits<{ delete: [id: string] }>()

const displayName = computed(() =>
  `${user.value.firstName} ${user.value.lastName}`
)
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-4 p-4 rounded-lg bg-white shadow-sm">
    <span class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-900">{{ displayName }}</span>
    <button
      v-if="!isLoading"
      class="px-3 py-1 text-sm bg-blue-600 text-white rounded hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors"
      @click="emit('delete', user.id)"
    >Delete</button>
  </div>
</template>
```

### Component Rules

- File and component names: **PascalCase** (`UserCard.vue`).
- Max ~200 lines per component; split into sub-components otherwise.
- Props always typed (`defineProps` or `defineModel`). Prefer `defineModel()` for v-model.
- Emits always typed via `defineEmits<{...}>()`.
- No `any` types.
- Extract logic beyond 2–3 computed/refs into a composable (SRP).

## Composables — Composition Pattern

Composables are the primary logic-composition mechanism in Vue 3 — GoF **Composition Pattern**.

```typescript
// composables/useUser.ts
// Pattern: Composition — reusable stateful logic decoupled from UI

/**
 * Fetch and expose a single user by ID.
 *
 * @param userId - Reactive user ID; re-fetches automatically on change.
 * @returns Reactive user data, loading state, error, and derived fullName.
 */
export function useUser(userId: Ref<string>) {
  const { data: user, isLoading, error } = useFetch<User>(
    computed(() => `/api/users/${userId.value}`)
  )
  const fullName = computed(() =>
    user.value ? `${user.value.firstName} ${user.value.lastName}` : ''
  )
  return { user, isLoading, error, fullName }
}
```

- Name starts with `use` (`useUser`, `useAuth`, `useNotifications`).
- Returns reactive data — never plain values.
- One composable = one concern (SRP).
- Test composables independently of components (`@vue/test-utils` not required).

## Docstrings — TSDoc Style

Every exported function, composable, and class has a TSDoc comment:

```typescript
/**
 * Fetch paginated list of documents from the API.
 *
 * @param page - 1-based page number.
 * @param pageSize - Number of items per page. Defaults to 20.
 * @returns Reactive object with `data`, `total`, `isLoading`, `error`.
 *
 * @example
 * const { data, isLoading } = useDocuments(page, 20)
 */
export function useDocuments(page: Ref<number>, pageSize = 20) { ... }
```

- Types are not repeated in JSDoc (they are in the TypeScript signature) — describe semantics only.
- Add `@example` for composables and utility functions with non-trivial usage.
- Document Props interfaces with an inline comment above each prop.

## Pinia Store

```typescript
// stores/auth.ts
export const useAuthStore = defineStore('auth', () => {
  const user = ref<User | null>(null)
  const isAuthenticated = computed(() => user.value !== null)

  async function login(credentials: LoginCredentials) {
    user.value = await authApi.login(credentials)
  }
  function logout() { user.value = null }

  return { user, isAuthenticated, login, logout }
})
```

- Prefer **Setup store** (function syntax) over Options store.
- One store = one domain area.

## Tailwind CSS v4

```css
/* src/assets/main.css */
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  --color-brand: #2563eb;
}
```

```vue
<!-- ✅ Utility-first — no custom CSS for trivial styles -->
<div class="flex flex-col gap-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">Title</h1>
</div>
```

- Responsive prefixes: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` — mobile-first.
- Dark mode: `dark:` prefix (class strategy).
- Avoid inline styles (`style="..."`). `@apply` only for repeated component patterns.

## Performance

- Lazy-load routes: `component: () => import('./pages/Dashboard.vue')`.
- Lazy-load heavy components: `defineAsyncComponent(() => import('./HeavyChart.vue'))`.
- `v-memo` for expensive render lists.
- `computed` instead of methods for derived data — auto-cached.

## Testing

- **Vitest** for unit tests.
- **Vue Test Utils** for component testing.
- **Playwright** for E2E. Cypress only as an explicit exception.

```typescript
import { mount } from '@vue/test-utils'
import UserCard from '@/components/UserCard.vue'

test('displays full name', () => {
  const wrapper = mount(UserCard, {
    props: { user: { id: '1', firstName: 'Jan', lastName: 'Novák' } },
  })
  expect(wrapper.text()).toContain('Jan Novák')
})
```

## .gitignore — Node/Vue-Specific Entries

Add these to the project `.gitignore` when Node.js / Vue / Vite is used:

```gitignore
node_modules/
dist/
.output/
.vite/
coverage/
*.local
.env.local
.env.*.local
```
